; One variable: a CanvasItemMaterial blend that lowers the canvas alpha. SUB writes
; `dst.a - src.a * src.a` and MUL `dst.a * src.a`, so a translucent item leaves alpha under 1.
; Godot reads an opaque viewport's alpha as 1 (`swizzle_a = ONE`, `texture_storage.cpp:3641-3642`),
; so nothing behind the canvas shows through. A ColorRect and a Polygon2D carry each mode.

